# Fact patterns — expense approval

Generated from `corpus/gold/fact_patterns.jsonl`. The interesting cases are the ones where
the corporate ladder and the Engineering ladder disagree and § 7.1 picks the stricter.

> Using Legal_types as T
> Using Expense_approval_acme as E

## FP-032 — both ladders agree

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestFp032:
  output computation content E.ExpenseApproval

scope TestFp032:
  definition computation equals
    output of E.ExpenseApproval with {
      -- amount: $800
      -- department: T.Department.Engineering
    }
  assertion computation.approval_level = T.ApprovalLevel.Manager
  assertion computation.receipt_required = true
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope TestFp032
┌─[RESULT]─ TestFp032 ─
│ computation =
│   ExpenseApproval {
│     -- approval_level: Manager
│     -- receipt_required: true
│   }
└─
```

